{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "lanes_surface_region",
    "description": "A pointwise loss on a 6 x 5 x 4 grid whose right-hand side is a whole-array makearray with a region one cell thick along a lane set: every cell loses k*A, and the surface layer (lev 1) a larger kd + k, written as a later region over lev 1..1 whose value is an array faq over (lon, lat) reading A at the literal lev 1 (the form of a planner's surface-only band coefficient). A lane's region depends on its cell, so a lane program reads it by region membership.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciAST test suite"
    ],
    "created": "2026-11-25T00:00:00Z",
    "tags": [
      "conformance",
      "range_restricted_rhs"
    ]
  },
